From 59b309113a53fde644e6d61dbc202ff0f926ebfa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: originaxiom <originaxiom@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 18:31:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/15] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's series 5, patch 3;
 first built on 5c7abd72a; built again on main's bf76e5ab1 with the 41 patches
 of R80b, the ten patches of series 4, the move of the old front pages and the
 first two of series 5 applied): A ZONE CANNOT MOVE THE DAY BACK, AND THE
 GUARD ON THE DAY READS EVERY COMMIT (Review 79, the second reader's row 10,
 its first and second parts; the first reader's R79-SM-47). The day a gate
 judges by was the day the commit states, in the commit's own zone. The guard
 on that day read the commit's time. A commit made one second after its parent
 and stated in a zone twelve hours behind, after a parent stated fourteen
 hours ahead, passed the guard and moved the day two days back. And the guard
 read main's own line only: a commit dated before its parent on a branch that
 is then merged, and a merge dated before the branch it merges, were not read.
 THE MEND: the day a commit is judged on is the later of two days, the day in
 UTC of the commit's time and the day the commit states. It is worked out in
 the one module that decides the day, and the gates and the date of a review's
 anchor take the same. So the day is never earlier than the day of a time
 which the guard holds to be no earlier than any parent's: a zone cannot move
 it back. A day stated ahead is kept. The day an age is counted from, in the
 checker of leads, is the day in UTC of the commit's time, which a zone cannot
 move forward: so no zone makes a debt younger from either end. The guard
 reads every commit that the head reaches and its root does not, each beside
 each of its parents. WHAT MOVES ON MAIN: nothing. Main's zone is ahead of
 UTC, so the day each of its commits states is the later of the two, and the
 debt gates read at main's head as they did. FOUND BEFORE SENDING, AND KEPT:
 as first built the day was the day in UTC alone, everywhere. Three of main's
 38 commits after the rule's root were made in the first hour after midnight
 in main's zone, and one of them is the anchor of Review 79, entered at 00:22
 on the 12th. Its day became the 11th. The owner's waiver typed on the 11th,
 which had expired when the review was entered, covered again, and the gate on
 the review would not have fired before 50 landings. One of main's own tests,
 test_the_waiver_file_exists_with_the_grammar_and_no_live_waiver, failed on
 that build and was not run when the patch was first made; it was found when
 the ninth patch was. The dates typed on main's pages are days in main's zone,
 and a day read from a commit is compared with them: that is why the day
 stated is kept where it is the later. On main no commit after the root is
 dated before a parent, on any line: there is no other line after the root.
 The comment in the relay checker that said the day cannot stand still says
 what the guard bounds: a run of commits each dated at its parent's time keeps
 the day still. That is a comment, and it has no test. Four lines of the first
 series' lock that read the day as the commit states it now read it as the
 gates do, each with a dated note. What it does not reach: between a parent's
 time and the real time a commit's time is its maker's to choose, as before. A
 commit that states a zone ahead of UTC is judged a day later for as many
 hours as that zone is ahead, which makes a debt older and never younger. The
 lock: three tests added to tests/test_gates_are_a_function_of_the_commit.py.
 On the commit before, two fail: the day of a commit made a second after its
 parent is earlier than its parent's and the guard passes; and a commit dated
 a month before its parent, merged from a branch, is read by nothing. The
 third holds the first hour after midnight; on the commit before it cannot
 run, since it names what this patch adds, and the behaviour it holds stood
 there: it is a twin against this patch's own first build. Tested against
 planted errors; computed once. 0 of 19.

